        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T15:22:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we add a check for bp2build that we can\u0027t have multiple attributes with the same name so that we don\u0027t end up with `data` attrs coming from multiple places? (e.g. as is occurring in python/sh currently)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 403,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 403,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "75b294d7b70df6c88850aaf5408fc4a13078a90d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d806a4e_dd988278",
        "filename": "bp2build/build_conversion.go",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 403,
      "author": {
        "id": 1887575
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T15:29:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could do so, but that would require reflection, which I thought we were trying to entirely avoid. Or do you mean inside of `extractModuleProperties` we should dedupe and merge existing values (or just error-out)? In the former case, I\u0027d carry over some of the old reflection logic I had.",
      "parentUuid": "bde1bfa0_1f999c07",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 403,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 403,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "75b294d7b70df6c88850aaf5408fc4a13078a90d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6277bf4_2b81e1a6",
        "filename": "bp2build/build_conversion.go",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 403,
      "author": {
        "id": 1887575
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T16:48:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Also, this sort of thing is why I take a reference to the actual `attrs.Data` so I can keep `.Append`ing. That\u0027s the style I expect for all multiply-used, list-based attrs.",
      "parentUuid": "4d806a4e_dd988278",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 403,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 403,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "75b294d7b70df6c88850aaf5408fc4a13078a90d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3551da22_68a13cd1",
        "filename": "bp2build/build_conversion.go",
        "patchSetId": 32
      },
      "lineNbr": 403,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687194
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T17:17:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "By check, I meant do a validation check for duplicate attribute names and error out if duplicate attribute names are found. A check like this would enforce specifying common attributes in CommonAttributes.\n\nIf we do add this check, a natural place to do this would be within extractModuleProperties itself as implementing it there  wouldn\u0027t require additional reflection. extractModuleProperties is populating a map of attribute name : attribute BUILD-ified string, so the check should be straightforward when populating that map. It may be incompatible with queryview, so we may need a parameter, e.g. allowDuplicateProperties, to know whether to error/not.",
      "parentUuid": "b6277bf4_2b81e1a6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 403,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 403,
        "endChar": 33
      },
